			"date": "2023-03-08T23:02:36.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fosstodon.org/@eleventy\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>eleventy</span></a></span> It's tough for brand accounts to make the move and I think it's a sound strategy to have a presence on both sites for now. There's a very real possibility that Twitter won't exist in a few years, either die to technical or regulatory woes. Creating a mastodon presence steadily now in conjunction with a Twitter one is going to go a long way if/when they finally shut down for good</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
